WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
And Illinois Congressman is urging NHTSA to investigate Tesla autopilot and FSD after videos show drivers asleep. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 606. The request targets NHTSA oversight of the systems. The videos depict multiple instances of drivers not paying attention while the vehicle operates under the supervised software. The Congressman wants regulators to examine whether current driver monitoring features

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:45.200
are sufficient to prevent misuse. The call adds to ongoing scrutiny of how Tesla's assisted driving technology is being used on public roads. While US scrutiny intensifies, one European country is moving in the opposite direction.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:53.760
Slovenia's Deputy Prime Minister said the country will update its laws to allow robotaxies after personally testing Tesla FSD.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:01:08.280
The official experience the supervised system on public roads and concluded that current technology is ready for broader deployment. Lawmakers are now working on specific rules that would permit unsupervised robotaxies services in the future.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:14.160
The announcement positions Slovenia as one of the earlier European countries to move on this issue.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:36.080
Regulatory progress abroad pairs with Tesla's own hardware timeline for unsupervised capability. Tesla ties unsupervised operation to its next-generation inference chip rather than existing silicon. This creates a two-track timeline where supervised FSD advances on current hardware while unsupervised waits on new chips.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:48.300
The decision affects fleet consistency, regulatory approvals, and when higher margin service revenue can scale. That hardware dependency makes Tesla's manufacturing footprint even more relevant.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:58.160
Tesla is evaluating Fort Bend County in Texas for a potential solar manufacturing facility. The project would expand the company's solar production footprint.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:14.080
Local officials have been in discussions with Tesla about the site selection and potential economic impact. The facility would complement existing solar panel and solar roof production elsewhere in the United States. No final decision or timeline has been announced yet.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:27.620
Solar production growth sits alongside rising demand for stationary storage. The on-grid battery energy storage systems market is projected to reach $141.37 billion by 2035.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:37.780
Tesla energy products form part of this expanding segment. Growth is driven by increasing renewable energy integration and grid stabilization needs worldwide.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:50.080
Utility scale projects using megapack style systems are expected to account for a significant share of the total. While energy storage scales, the CyberCab continues its global showcase tour.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:03:00.420
Tesla's CyberCab tour begins in Sydney as the first stop in Australia. The vehicle is making appearances across multiple locations without operating on public roads.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:12.980
The tour showcases the two-seater autonomous design to local audiences and media. Organizers have confirmed the CyberCab will travel to additional cities but will remain off public roads during demonstrations.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:20.280
The events allow potential customers and regulators to view the vehicle up close ahead of any future regulatory approvals.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:33.400
Tesla Roddy posted about loving the launch series Puddle Lights on the Tesla Model YL. The account suggests Tesla should add these to every car, even just the T logo, since badging has been removed from models.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:43.080
The feature illuminates the ground beside the vehicle when approaching or exiting. Owners have expressed interest in seeing the lights become a standard offering across the lineup.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:56.660
The post highlights how the lights enhance the vehicle's premium feel at night. Tesla Roddy noted that steering on the Model YL feels more responsive than on their Model Y, with the wheel easier to turn and a sportier feel.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:02.120
They also said they would retrofit a black headliner into their own Model Y if possible.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:13.360
The steering change gives the larger vehicle a more agile character during daily driving. The headliner preference points to interior customization options that some owners are already considering.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.980
The impressions came from direct time spent with the Model YL variant.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:33.200
Tesla posted that FSD supervised with GROC is a lot like having your own robotaxi. The comparison emphasizes how the combination of supervised autonomy and the in-car AI assistant creates a hands-off experience for the driver.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:40.360
Owners can interact with GROC for navigation, entertainment and vehicle controls while the system handles the road.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:51.920
The post positions the current software stack as a preview of future unsupervised operation. It underscores Tesla's view that the integration already delivers meaningful convenience today.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:05:02.460
A non-Tesla DC fast charger ranked highest in JD Power's public EV charging study. The result highlights competition in the open access charging space.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:11.400
Tesla's Supercharger network still serves the majority of Tesla owners but now faces direct comparisons on reliability and user experience.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:24.140
The study evaluated multiple networks on factors including speed, uptime and ease of payment. The top-ranked networks performance shows that other providers are closing the gap in customer satisfaction metrics.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:33.640
Tesla is preparing to enter an additional Asian market to grow its regional operations. The move follows recent subsidiary setups in other Asian countries.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:40.860
Company filings indicate plans to establish local entities that can handle sales, service and regulatory compliance.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:48.020
The expansion aims to capture growing demand for electric vehicles in markets that have not yet seen significant Tesla presence.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:57.820
Details on the specific country remain limited in public announcements. A Tesla owner attempted to use summon in a parking lot and the vehicle collided with another car.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:08.320
The incident prompted online warnings about relying on the feature. The owner had activated the summon function from outside the vehicle, expecting it to navigate the space safely.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:16.040
Video of the event circulated widely and led to renewed discussion about the current limitations of the low speed maneuvering system.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:27.980
Tesla has not commented publicly on the specific case. Tesla began selling semi-chargers in five European countries. The chargers support the upcoming European semi-deployments.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:35.120
Fleet operators can now purchase the dedicated charging hardware ahead of vehicle deliveries scheduled for 2027.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:45.740
The move prepares the infrastructure needed for long haul electric trucking across the region. Sales are currently limited to approved commercial customers, rather than individual buyers.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:56.380
Hyundai is working to close the gap as Tesla increases its share of South Korea's electric vehicle sales. Tesla's models continue to outsell local competitors in the market.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:07:09.340
The company has maintained strong demand for the Model Y and Model 3 despite new entrants from domestic manufacturers. Hyundai has responded with updated models and pricing adjustments aimed at regaining ground.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:15.040
Market data shows Tesla's lead has widened over the past year in the premium EV segment.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:25.640
Tesla now shows insurance cost estimates on its vehicle order page. Buyers can adjust mileage and coverage options to see potential savings tied to FSD usage.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:37.340
The tool lets customers compare rates with and without the supervised autonomy package. Insurance partners have begun recognizing FSD as a factor that can lower premiums in select markets.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:43.160
The feature gives buyers a clearer picture of ongoing ownership costs before finalizing a purchase.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:53.000
Buid unveiled the ETT-44 electric semi with a 651 kilowatt hours battery and megawatt charging capability.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:08:03.240
The truck is scheduled for European availability soon. The 372 mile range figure is based on real-world testing conditions rather than laboratory estimates.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:10.020
Megawatt charging support allows the vehicle to add substantial range in under an hour at compatible stations.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:15.620
The launch directly challenges Tesla's semi in the European heavy-duty EV segment.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:25.040
XCorp and SpaceX AI dropped their antitrust lawsuit against Apple. Open AI remains the sole defendant in the ongoing case.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:34.080
The settlement removes one defendant from the multi-company complaint that alleged anti-competitive behavior in the AI and app distribution markets.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:39.360
Legal proceedings against open AI are expected to continue on the original timeline.

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:48.040
The move narrows the scope of the litigation while keeping pressure on the remaining party. In-car AI features are also evolving in the meantime.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:54.540
Grok integration in Tesla vehicles will add the ability to send text messages on behalf of the driver.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:04.700
Additional functions are planned for the in-car assistant. The update builds on the existing voice interaction that already handles navigation, media, and climate controls.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:11.680
Tesla has indicated that more productivity-oriented features will roll out through software updates over the coming months.

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:21.120
Not every software story is smooth, however. A California homeowner reported that Tesla's solar panel output dropped to one quarter of normal levels.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.360
The repair request has since stalled without resolution from the company.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.720
Tesla has not provided an updated timeline for addressing the issue.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:36.480
The customer has followed up multiple times through the service portal, but has received only automated acknowledgments.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:44.460
The case illustrates ongoing challenges some solar owners face when system performance declines and warranty support is required.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:51.020
Before we go, the Fort Bend County discussions could clarify whether the solar expansion moves forward.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.720
That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:10:03.940
TSLA closed at $358.97, down $6.47, or 1.8%.

